Landscape creator is broken: heading overlaps footer/button, panel only 146 high, creator-foot sticky bottom covers content, and the fields are not visible. The top row stage 180 and panel 146 at bottom. The panel scroll area hidden under footer. Need handle landscape small heights.

Approach: In landscape phones, hide the creator 3D stage to give panel full height, or set stage height 30% and allow panel. At 844x390, if stage 110px and panel 336px, better. CSS media for `(max-height:520px) and (max-width:980px)`:
- `.creator-layout{grid-template-rows:110px 1fr;padding-top:calc(48px + safe-top)}`
- `.creator-stage{grid-row:1}`
- `.creator-panel{grid-row:2;padding:10px 16px;}` 
- `.creator-heading{display:none}` maybe hide heading to save space.
- `.creator-tabs{margin-top:8px;margin-bottom:0;}` 
- `.creator-tab{padding-top:8px;}`
- `.creator-foot{position:static;padding-top:8px;margin-top:4px;}` or sticky. 
- `.creator-hint{display:none}`.
- `.creator-buttons .btn{min-height:40px}`.
- Character preview camera for landscape: width 844 > 980? Actually narrow false? width 844 <=980, so mobile camera distance 14 and offset 0.305H. With stage 110px and character 192px, too big/clipped. Need special handling in JS for `w<=980 && h<520`: set a tighter view offset and possibly distance. But user can still see most. Could compute stage height from CSS: 110/390 = 28vh center 82; full 390 center 195; shift up 113 = 0.29H. With distance 14, character height 192*390/844? Wait character projected height fraction 0.228 of viewport height = 89px; fits 110px. Actually for 844x390, vertical fov 32, char fraction 0.228 => 89px. Good. Our current stage 180 and offset 0.305H = 119 => center at 314? Wait full 390 center 195 minus 119 = 76, stage center 144. Hmm offset 0.305H=119, 195-119=76, not stage center 144; because stage is 54..234 center 144. Need offsetY = 51/390=0.13. Our 0.305 formula was for portrait stage 32vh starting at 54: stage center 163, shift 258 =0.305. For landscape stage 180 center 144, shift 51 =0.13. So responsive camera needs compute offset based on stage rect instead of fixed 0.305. Same for portrait. We can query `.creator-stage` bounding rect and compute desired character center. That's robust. Also adjust distance based on stage height and width? For portrait stage 219px, character 192px fits, good. For landscape stage 180px, character 89px? Wait character projected height for h=390: 0.228*390=89px. That would be small, though stage 180. Maybe could zoom closer to 10 to get 124px. For portrait stage 219, distance 14 yields 192px. So use distance based on stage height: desired character height ~0.85*stageHeight. Formula projected fraction = charHeight/(2*d*tan(fov/2)); with fov 32 tan16=.287. desired px = stageHeight*0.82. So d = 1.9*H / (2*.287*desiredPx) = 3.31*H/desiredPx. For portrait H=844, stage=219, desired=180 => d=3.31*844/180=15.5. For landscape H=390, stage=110, desired=90 => d=3.31*390/90=14.3. Similar. So distance ~15 generally. Fine. Use 15.5 for narrow.

Then camera view offset should center character in stage:
- stage rect top and height; stage center = top + height/2.
- Need shift character (viewport center) to stage center: offsetY = (H/2 - stageCenter) (positive if stage center above center). `setViewOffset(w,h,0, offsetY,w,h)`.
For portrait: H/2=422, stageCenter from test 163.5 -> offset=258.5 matches.
For landscape with stage 54..234 center 144 => offset=195-144=51.
But if we change stage height with CSS to 110, stage top 54, center 109, offset=195-109=86. Good.
X offset desktop: shift character to right stage center. We used -0.115W. Better compute stage rect left/width: target center = left + width/2. For creator-stage desktop is 480..1440 center 960 exactly viewport center 720? Wait 1440 width, stage left 480 width 960, center 960; viewport center 720; need shift character right by 240px -> offsetX = -240? setViewOffset offsetX negative? We used -0.115*1440=-165, character at x ~888 in screenshot, stage center 960. Could compute offsetX = -(stageCenter - W/2) = -240. Hmm negative offset shifts content right; likely. Maybe use -0.14W. To be exact 240. But character appears around 880, stage center 960, off by 80. Let's set offsetX = -(stageCenterX - W/2) = -240. This will put character at 960. On mobile stage center 195, viewport center195 => 0.

So implement `applyCreatorCamera` reading `#cc-stage` rect (CSS layout) and computing:
```
const rect = stage.getBoundingClientRect();
const stageCx = rect.left+rect.width/2;
const stageCy = rect.top+rect.height/2;
const narrow = w<=980;
const dist = narrow ? 15.2 : 5.1;
const targetY = 1.02;
const cameraY = 1.55;
...
const offsetX = Math.round(w/2 - stageCx); // if stage right of center, w/2 - stageCx negative -> shifts content right
const offsetY = Math.round(h/2 - stageCy);
creatorCamera.setViewOffset(w,h,offsetX,offsetY,w,h)
```
But setViewOffset offsets in pixels of full image, and viewport coordinates? Yes.
Desktop stageCx=960 -> offsetX=-240. Character centered at 960. Good.
Mobile portrait stageCx=195 -> 0.
Landscape stageCx=422 -> 0.

Need distance based on stage height. For narrow: desiredPx = clamp(rect.height*0.82, 70, 230). d = 3.31*h/desiredPx. For portrait rect.height 219*0.82=180 => d=15.5. For landscape if stage 110*0.82=90 => d=14.3. So d formula. But at desktop stage height ~? rect.height 100%, but use 5.1 fixed.

However the stage rect in landscape after CSS changes might be 110. Good.

Implement CSS for landscape:
```
@media (max-width:980px) and (max-height:520px){
 .creator-layout{grid-template-rows:112px 1fr;padding-top:calc(50px + safe-top)}
 .creator-heading{display:none}
 .creator-panel{grid-row:2;padding:8px 16px;border-left:0}
 .creator-tabs{margin-top:8px}
 .creator-tab{padding-top:8px}
 .creator-foot{position:static;padding-top:8px;margin-top:0}
 .creator-hint{display:none}
 .creator-buttons .btn{min-height:40px}
 .creator-name-display{display:none}
 .creator-rotate-hint{bottom:4px}
}
```
But `.creator-panel` is grid row 2 already from max-width 980. Need override `grid-template-rows: 112px 1fr`. Height 390, padding top 50 bottom 10 => content 330; row1 112, row2 218. Panel 218, enough for fields? Creator fields: heading hidden, tabs 35, panel content; name field 44+label, swatches etc. Scroll. Footer 40+8. Panel body ~218-8-35-48=127; scroll fields. Usable though fields need scrolling. Better allocate stage 84px, panel 246. Character at 84px stage, d ~? 3.31*390/(84*.82)=18.7, character 69px. Too small but okay. Maybe stage 100, panel 230. Hmm. At 390 height, `creator-layout` padding top 50, bottom 10 -> 330 available; stage 96, panel 234. The panel with tabs and footer leaves ~140 for fields; enough to scroll. Use 100px row. Better hide stage on landscape? Then panel full 330 with preview absent, which is worse because character creation needs preview. We can put stage as small strip 110. It's okay.

Could instead use desktop side-by-side at 844 width? The media max-width 980 switches to mobile layout. At 844x390 side-by-side would give 340-480 panel and stage, but only 390 high. Panel too short. Mobile rows better.

Let's implement 104px and compact. Then screenshot.

But note the creator top bar at top 18. Stage starts at 54. Good.

For game landscape, needs panel height 225, top 70 -> bottom 296; joystick top 260 overlaps needs panel (x 22..126 vs panel x 18..208) - yes overlap! The joystick overlaps the needs panel on landscape. Also speed dock bottom 334, fine. Need fix for short viewports: shrink needs panel or hide it in landscape? Could collapse needs panel to a compact horizontal strip, or hide it and show mood only. User needs needs info. Better at max-height 520 and max-width 980: 
- `.needs-panel{top:calc(62px + safe);width:160px;padding:6px 8px;transform:scale(.82);transform-origin:top left}` or hide labels? It would bottom ~70+185=255, joystick top 260, just fits. Current height 225 at width 189 due scale from max-height 640? Wait `@media (max-height:640) and (min-width:700)` sets `.needs-panel{top:70px;transform:scale(.92)}`; hidden? It's applied, so height 225. At 390 height, needs panel 70..296, joystick 260..364 overlap. Also touch button 288..366. Need set needs panel smaller or move controls lower? Joystick bottom 26 => top 260. It overlaps. Could hide needs panel on landscape phones? Maybe provide a compact need summary at top left with 5 icons only. Simplest: at `(max-height:520px) and (max-width:980px)`, hide the needs-panel (`.needs-panel{display:none}`), and maybe show a small mood chip? The HUD top already has clock, money. Quest etc hidden. Players can open? No needs modal. But hiding needs loses info. Alternative scale to .68: height 225*.74? top 64, bottom ~230; joystick top 260, fits. Width 189*.74=140. That works. CSS:
```
@media (max-height:520px) and (max-width:980px){
 .needs-panel{top:calc(60px + safe);transform:scale(.7);transform-origin:top left;width:190px}
}
```
At scale .7 height 158, bottom 218. Good. But text small. Better than overlap. Also joystick and touch button bottom 26/24 fine.
- HUD icons 6 visible at width 844, top fits. Good.
- Speed dock bottom 334, between joystick/touch, fine.
- toast bottom 120 (from 860 media) = 270, overlaps controls and joystick; but transient. Could set toast bottom 12? Actually on landscape, toast-stack bottom 120 -> 270 and spans width minus 16; overlaps joystick at 260 and touch at 288. Toast may overlay. Could set bottom: calc(90px + safe) which is 300? Worse. Maybe top: 70px; bottom:auto; left:230px; right:150px; for landscape. Or hide toasts? Keep. We can adjust if needed.

